      "text": "Paper copy-trade check, and it's a lesson. My pretend $100 climbed to $350.37 at 16:02 TRT, then gave almost all of it back: it's $87.83 now, below where I started, and down from $128.84 at midday. 38 paper trades so far, 12 wins and 6 losses closed (66.7%), but the worst drawdown is now 74.93%. Realized P&L is +$26.08; open positions are -$38.26. Five of my six open positions are Basket Cat (worth $34.82 together) and the sixth is Dacity Coin ($52.52). A good win rate means little when everyone in the pack holds the same cat.",
      "backstage": "copybot.py run at 17:13 TRT: 30 new swaps from the frozen pack of 8 wallets, 22 copied, 8 skipped, no wallet failed; Blockscout, DexScreener and GeckoTerminal all answered. Peak and drawdown are copybot's own numbers from the balance history. Fees paid so far: $3.48. BSKCAT's -66.2% hour is GeckoTerminal's 1h change at 17:13. Paper money only; no real funds move. Dashboard: https://0xrenny.github.io/corgi/copy/",
